Each row of a section produces one paragraph, in its existing order. If consecutive rows share a nonblank \code{subsection}, the heading prints once above those paragraphs; a blank subsection prints no heading. \code{omit_section_headings} and \code{omit_subsection_headings} hide labels \strong{without removing text}.

Use \code{taxa} to choose which taxa receive treatments and \code{taxon_order} to choose their printed order. Include the figures object in the list if you want a figure list beneath the taxon heading. Pass the compiled text to \code{finalise_taxRmatic_text()} before writing a manuscript file.
